{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067178-airbending-practices","id":1067178,"title":"Airbending Practices?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-23T14:28:05-07:00","id":1067178,"title":"Airbending Practices?","content":"What Forces Practices would you need to pull airbending feats from the Avatar series? Would Forces 3 be enough to do most of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:52:12-07:00","id":1067188,"title":"","content":"Yup. <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(characters)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:01:52-07:00","id":1067195,"title":"","content":"Or Matter 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:35:47-07:00","id":1067211,"title":"","content":"Practice of Ruling (2 dots) is enough to perform most tricks by simply commanding the Wind to do what you desire, using Forces.<br /> Though you might find it a bit difficult to use if the winds are low and there's little energy to work with.<br /> Practice of Weaving (3 dots) however can enhance the strength of the airflow, allowing you to perform most of the tricks you'll see in the show.<br /> <br /> In comparison to this, the Shaping spell of Matter 2 can control the movement of air (as well as water, and earth if you use Reach) entirely in keeping with the abilitie of the show, regardless of if there's any airflow or not. So I'd personally go with Matter over Forces. Or perhaps even grab both. At which point you're practically the Avatar with control over Fire, Water, Earth, Air, as well as all of the specialist types such as Lightning, Lava, and spontaneous Combustion.<br /> <br /> Combine that with a &quot;Shaper&quot; Shadow Name and you've got a potent yantra for use with any spell that rearranges the fundamental element building blocks of the Cosmos.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:59:49-07:00","id":1067693,"title":"","content":"Throw in the Adamant Hand and Kung Fu FS merits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T19:15:22-07:00","id":1067888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067178-airbending-practices?p=1067693#post1067693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Throw in the Adamant Hand and Kung Fu FS merits...</div> </div> </div> </div>My Shadow Name Merit already covers my focus in Air Magic.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the help guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12979-one-dawn","name":"One Dawn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}